{"id": 69, "ts": 1780451126.9496756, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s enthusiasm for Candidate\u202fC, especially his ability to make rapid, correct decisions and stay calm during a crisis. Those are certainly valuable for long\u2011distance operations. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit. B is very conscientious, handles stress exceptionally well, and excels at assessing weather conditions\u2014critical for international routes. His excellent computer skills also support the complex avionics we use. While B does have a relatively weak memory for numbers and has been noted to make nasty remarks to colleagues, the memory issue can be mitigated by standard cross\u2011check procedures, and his overall professionalism and reliability outweigh the interpersonal slip, especially given his strong stress resilience and conscientiousness. In contrast, C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability, which are essential for safe, long\u2011haul flights. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
